**/*.md
**/CHANGELOG*
**/.github/**
**/*.map
**/*.d.ts

# `@terrastruct/d2`'s browser entry (dist/browser) is the only build seemore ever loads — the
# app aliases straight to it, and the CLI process itself never imports the package directly.
# The Node builds are dead weight here (~50MB) but stay in the tarball we ship on npm, where
# a consumer may run seemore outside a bundler and need them.
node_modules/@terrastruct/d2/dist/node-esm/**
node_modules/@terrastruct/d2/dist/node-cjs/**

# mermaid's `exports` map only ever resolves to dist/mermaid.core.mjs (plus its on-demand
# dist/chunks/*). These are its `<script>`-tag UMD/IIFE bundles, unreachable through the
# package's own module resolution, and only add weight here.
node_modules/mermaid/dist/mermaid.js
node_modules/mermaid/dist/mermaid.min.js
node_modules/mermaid/dist/mermaid.esm.mjs
node_modules/mermaid/dist/mermaid.esm.min.mjs
